@startuml

title Client Credentials: a service acts as itself

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
autonumber


participant "a service" as svc
participant "token provider\n(in the service)" as prov
participant "IAM" as iam
participant "another service" as svc2

== startup, after the service's own subjects are subscribed ==
prov -> iam : iam.v1.auth.service-login\n(the service's own account)
iam --> prov : token for the service: no party,\nthe service account's permissions
== every call the service makes as itself ==
svc -> prov : the token
alt more than 20% of its life left
    prov --> svc : the cached token
else close to expiry
    prov -> iam : log in again
    iam --> prov : a new token
    prov --> svc : the new token
end
svc -> svc2 : request (Authorization: the service's token)
svc2 --> svc : response for the service's own scope

@enduml
